# Packages for the Gaming Live CD.
#
# One package name per line; lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# BuildRoot requires every listed package to exist as a binary package in
# the Packages directory (see bin/BuildRoot). Build the recipes with
# CreatePackage after compiling each one.
#
# Build order matters for the kernel modules: Linux first, then Nvidia
# (its recipe compiles modules against the installed kernel).

Linux
Glibc
Glibc-32

# 32-bit X11 libraries (Steam client + games UI)
Lib32-X11
Lib32-Xext
Lib32-Xrandr
Lib32-Xinerama
Lib32-Xcursor
Lib32-Xi
Lib32-Xcomposite
Lib32-Xdamage
Lib32-Xss
Lib32-Xfixes
Lib32-Xtst

# 32-bit system libraries
Lib32-DBus
Lib32-FreeType
Lib32-Fontconfig
Lib32-libpng
Lib32-zlib
Lib32-libxml2
Lib32-expat
Lib32-libxcb
Lib32-libgcc
Lib32-libstdcpp

# 32-bit audio libraries (Wine/Proton sound)
Lib32-alsa-lib
Lib32-libpulse
Lib32-libsndfile

# 32-bit keyboard handling
Lib32-xkbcommon

# 32-bit GL/Vulkan dispatch + Mesa (Wine/Proton rendering)
Lib32-libglvnd
Lib32-mesa
Lib32-vulkan-loader

# 32-bit SDL2 (games + Steam)
Lib32-SDL2

# Vulkan SDK
Vulkan-Headers
Vulkan-Loader
Vulkan-Tools

# NVIDIA driver (64+32-bit, kernel modules, Vulkan ICD)
Nvidia

# Steam client
Steam

# Wine is a source-build alternative to the prebuilt Proton used with Steam;
# if built, uncomment the next line:
#Wine
#
# Proton itself is not a separate package: a prebuilt Proton (e.g.
# GE-Proton11-3) is baked into the Steam package via "bin/AddProton" and ships
# in /Users/root/.local/share/Steam/compatibilitytools.d/.
